.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# This repo is PUBLIC (github.com/Rtyson47/cieinsider) and its root is the deployed web root, so
# anything committed here is readable at cieinsider.com/<path> as well as on GitHub.
# Added 2026-07-30, when bridge/ was about to be committed wholesale.

# Internal verification reports: they quote blockers, unverified-claim post-mortems and
# accountant/VAT notes. They belong next to the asset for working purposes, never on the site.
**/verification-report.md

# Archived page versions, kept per the versioning convention. Useful in the workspace, but in a
# web root they are publicly readable orphan pages carrying superseded copy.
**/_v[0-9]*.html

# Added 2026-08-05, while shipping the bridge practice generator. Same reason as above: the
# repo root is the web root, so each of these would be publicly fetchable if committed.

# Internal working docs. SEO audits and post-mortems quote blockers and unverified claims;
# they are for the workspace, not for cieinsider.com/docs/seo-indexing-audit-v2.md.
docs/
learnings/

# Local preview config. Machine-specific, and CLAUDE.md already records the canonical setup.
.claude/

# YouTube thumbnail sources: funnel assets, not site pages. They render as orphan pages in a
# web root and are not linked from anywhere.
_thumbs/

# Past paper PDFs staged but never registered in mcq/papers/index.json. Every paper the trainer
# actually serves IS committed (64 of 64 registered, checked 2026-08-05); these are extras that
# would publish CIE-copyright PDFs on the domain for no functional gain.
# Listed one by one ON PURPOSE. A blanket mcq/papers rule would silently swallow the next paper
# you add and register, which is a trap worth avoiding.
mcq/papers/0625/2021_m/
mcq/papers/0625/2021_s/
mcq/papers/0625/2021_w/
mcq/papers/0625/2022_m/
mcq/papers/0625/2022_s/
mcq/papers/0625/2022_w/
mcq/papers/9702/2021_m/
mcq/papers/9702/2021_s/
mcq/papers/9702/2021_w/
